ame>AKITA MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>EGUCHI SHINZO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIGASHI KAZUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAMETANI YASUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KANAYAMA SHINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MINAMITANI SHOZO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAMOTO KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUJISAWA TAKAFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WADA HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AKITA, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>EGUCHI, SHINZO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIGASHI, KAZUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAMETANI, YASUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANAYAMA, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MINAMITANI, SHOZO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAMOTO, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUJISAWA, TAKAFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WADA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>When an electrode (13) of an electronic component (150) and an electrode (21) of a circuit board (20) is joined together via bumps (11, 12) by relatively vibrating the electronic component and the circuit board, a periodic damping detection device (140) and a judging device (141) are used to detect a periodic damping caused by a progress of joining between the bumps and the electrodes and a success or failure of the joining is judged based on the periodic damping. In addition, a waveform during the joining in terms of an impedance, a moving distance of a nozzle (93) or a supply current to a VCM (121) in an ultrasonic oscillator (133) is compared to that of an acceptable product for judging an acceptability. The above constitution makes it possible to judge a success or failure of joining between the electronic component and the circuit board during the joining and moreover to prevent a defective product with an enhanced yield because a joining condition can be changed during the joining if a joining condition is found deteriorated.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Lorsque l'on assemble l'électrode (13) d'un composant électronique (150) et l'électrode (21) d'une carte imprimée (20) par l'intermédiaire de bosses (11, 12) en faisant relativement vibrer ce composant électronique et cette carte imprimée, on utilise un dispositif de détection d'amortissement périodique (140) et un dispositif d'évaluation (141) pour détecter tout amortissement périodique pouvant être provoqué par l'assemblage en cours entre les bosses et les électrodes, la réussite ou l'échec de cet assemblage étant évalués sur la base dudit amortissement périodique. On compare en outre la forme d'onde produite au cours de cet assemblage en termes d'impédance, de la distance variable d'une buse (93), ou d'un courant d'alimentation à un VCM (121) dans un oscillateur à ultrasons (133), à la forme d'onde d'un produit acceptable, de manière à estimer l'acceptabilité. La structure susmentionnée permet donc d'évaluer si l'assemblage entre le composant électronique et la carte imprimée est un échec ou une réussite, et également d'empêcher toute obtention d'un produit défectueux avec un rendement amélioré, l'assemblage pouvant en effet être modifié en cours de route si celui-ci s'avère détérioré.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>